From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Verm <183540171+vermingov@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 03:03:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 09/13] feat(linux): extension captures and downloads, page
 fullscreen, WebRTC and WebGPU

- tabs.captureVisibleTab and Firefox's tabs.captureTab: WebKit's snapshot
  of a tab the extension may read, cropped and scaled, as a PNG data URL.
- downloads.download: read in the extension's own context and sent in
  pieces within the channel's bound, then saved inside the Downloads
  folder (~/Downloads when none is configured), never over a file.
- Popups follow their page's size while open.
- Element fullscreen, switched off on Linux pending a broker: WebKitGTK's
  enter and leave signals feed the same ledger as on Windows, the page
  fills the window and the window follows; Escape on the window or the
  host asks the page to leave.
- WebRTC and WebGPU, off by default in WebKitGTK, are switched on for
  tabs (WebRTC takes effect where WebKitGTK is built with it).
